<title>FRANCE: Clinton would be elected by French, says survey.</title>
<headline>Clinton would be elected by French, says survey.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>French voters would overwhelmingly re-elect President Bill Clinton if they could cast ballots in the U.S. election, an opinion poll said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The survey in the weekly Le Point said 62 percent of 1,001 voters questioned would vote for Clinton and seven percent for Republican Bob Dole. Almost a third had no opinion.</p>
<p>The poll made no mention of Reform Party candidate Ross Perot.</p>
</text>
